  <prompt>
    Update LegalWorkspace (self-consumer) and WorkspaceLayoutWizard (if it consumes the section registry) to import from the new `@spaarke/legal-workspace` package. If task 021 chose re-export strategy (b), the existing LegalWorkspace-internal imports may keep working — verify. If task 021 chose move strategy (a), update all LegalWorkspace-internal imports to point at the new package.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE frontend build-engineer.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Both LegalWorkspace and WorkspaceLayoutWizard build correctly and consume the new shared package. Existing behavior preserved.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Complements task 022. After 022 + 023, all three consumers (SpaarkeAi, LegalWorkspace, WorkspaceLayoutWizard) build off the same shared package.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/package.json</file>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/vite.config.ts (if any alias)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/WorkspaceLayoutWizard/package.json</file>
      <file>src/solutions/WorkspaceLayoutWizard/vite.config.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Shared library SSOT.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Task 021's migration strategy dictates whether LegalWorkspace-internal imports change (a: yes, b: no).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
