  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read task 021's migration strategy decision from notes/fr10-migration-strategy.md.</step>
    <step order="2">If strategy (a) MOVE: update LegalWorkspace's internal imports (`src/sections/`, `sectionRegistry.ts`) to import from `@spaarke/legal-workspace` instead of relative paths.</step>
    <step order="3">If strategy (b) RE-EXPORT: verify LegalWorkspace's existing imports still work (they should — files stayed in place). Add file: dependency to `LegalWorkspace/package.json` so LegalWorkspace can also import from `@spaarke/legal-workspace` if desired (optional for LegalWorkspace-internal code but required if any LegalWorkspace file wants to use the canonical name).</step>
    <step order="4">Check WorkspaceLayoutWizard: does it consume section registry? Grep `sectionRegistry` in `WorkspaceLayoutWizard/`. If yes, add the new shared-package dependency to `WorkspaceLayoutWizard/package.json` + update imports.</step>
    <step order="5">Run `npm install` + `npm run build` in LegalWorkspace + WorkspaceLayoutWizard. Both succeed.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: 023 → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Install + build</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Edit + grep</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/package.json (modified — optional dependency addition)</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/WorkspaceLayoutWizard/package.json (modified — if consumer)</output>
